<title>THAILAND: Thai Airways gets 3 bln baht plane loan.</title>
<headline>Thai Airways gets 3 bln baht plane loan.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1996-08-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Thai Airways International Plc said on Friday it will borrow 3.0 billion baht from the Government Savings Bank to pay for a third Boeing 777-200 aircraft.</p>
<p>The airline said in a filing to the Stock Exchange of Thailand the Finance Ministry, which owns about 93 percent of Thai Airways' shares, will guarantee the transaction.</p>
<p>Thai Airways gave no further details on the purchase.</p>
<p>Under the 1995-2000 plan, Thai Airways plans to buy 21 airplanes pending approval by the Thai cabinet.</p>
<p>-- Bangkok newsroom (662) 652-0642</p>
